# Everyday talk (doc 30) by place and by region: the tavern, the chapel, the gate, the shore, the barracks, the
# hall, the market; then Ridgemere (the rain, the Sump, the wharf, the works, the Heights, the Houses) and the six towns
# and their country (doc 60). Alternatives are written in parallel.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Places

scene ev_pl_tavern_fire
when topic=smalltalk here.place=tavern
a : Shove over, let me near the fire. | This ale tastes of the barrel. | Who's paying for this round?
b[innkeeper] : Complaints go out the door. Coin goes on the counter.
b : There's room by the cat. | All ale tastes of barrel. | Not me. I paid last time.
a : The cat can shove over too. | Not like this. This is the barrel itself. | You never paid in your life.

scene ev_pl_tavern_late
when topic=smalltalk here.place=tavern here.time=night
a : One more and I'm going home. | I said one more an hour ago. | Is the landlord watering this?
b[innkeeper] : The landlord can hear you. And no.
b : You said that an hour ago. | And here we are. | Tastes like it.
a : I meant it then too. | Here we are indeed. | Tastes like puddle.

scene ev_pl_chapel_quiet
when topic=smalltalk here.place=chapel
a : It's peaceful in here. | The candles smell of honey. | I haven't been inside since I was a pup.
b[priest] : The doors are always open. Come more often.
b : Peaceful, and cold. | Beeswax. The good kind. | It hasn't changed.
a : Cold's good for the soul, they say. | Someone pays well for them. | Neither have I, much.

scene ev_pl_chapel_sermon
when topic=smalltalk here.place=chapel|street here.day=rest
a : Long sermon this morning. | Did you understand the sermon? | The priest was in a mood today.
b[priest] : I heard that. The Bright One heard it too.
b : My tail went numb. | Something about order and duty. | Somebody must've sinned.
a : Mine fell asleep entirely. | It's always that. | Not me. This week.

scene ev_pl_gate_queue
when topic=smalltalk here.place=gate
a : The gate line's longer every day. | Why do they search every cart? | Half the country's coming through here.
b[guard] : Because last week someone hid a stolen calf under the turnips.
b[carter] : Two hours I waited. Two hours!
b : Market day, maybe. | Orders. Always orders. | And leaving by noon.
a : Every day's market day now. | Somebody's orders. | Where are they all going?

scene ev_pl_gate_strangers
when topic=smalltalk here.place=gate
a : Strange scents on the road today. | Those travellers didn't smell like anywhere I know. | Lot of foreign tongues at the gate.
b[guard] : We note everyone who passes. Don't you worry.
b : From the far roads, maybe. | Southern, maybe. Spicy. | Trade's good.
a : Far roads. | Spice and dust. | Trade's good for someone.

scene ev_pl_shore
when topic=smalltalk here.place=shore
a : Water's cold enough to stop your heart. | Tide's out farther than I've ever seen. | Found a shell big as my paw.
b[fisher] : Low tide means a storm coming. Mark it.
b[sailor] : Seen bigger. Out in deep water, they're big as shields.
b : Don't swim, then. | Strange. | Keep it. Luck.
a : Wasn't planning on it. | It makes me uneasy. | I'll keep it on my sill.

scene ev_pl_barracks
when topic=smalltalk here.place=barracks
a : These cots were made for pups. | Who stole my good blanket? | Sergeant's in a foul temper.
b[soldier] : Complain to the quartermaster. He'll laugh at you.
b : Sleep on the floor, then. | Not me. | When isn't he?
a : The floor's warmer. | Somebody did. | Fair point.

scene ev_pl_hall
when topic=smalltalk here.place=hall
a : The council's sitting late again. | Look at the carvings on these beams. | It's always cold in the hall.
b[official] : Matters of state take time. As do petitions. As do you.
b : They love the sound of their voices. | Old work. Very old. | Big rooms always are.
a : More than we do. | Older than the town, they say. | And small purses.

scene ev_pl_market_haggle
when topic=smalltalk here.place=market
a : That cloth seller wanted a fortune. | I haggled her down by half! | Everything's a penny more than last market.
b[merchant] : And she'll still feed her pups. Haggling's a dance, not a war.
b : Walk away. They always call you back. | Teach me how. | Always is.
a : She didn't call me back. | Look sad. Very sad. | Always is.

scene ev_pl_market_crowd
when topic=smalltalk here.place=market here.day=market
a : I can't move for elbows today. | Mind your purse in this crush. | Everyone in the country's come to market.
b[guard] : Keep your coin in your fur, not your belt.
b : Market day. | Always do. | And their cousins.
a : I'll come early next time. | I'll keep a paw on it. | Their cousins' cousins.

scene ev_pl_home_chores
when topic=smalltalk here.place=home
a : The roof needs patching before the rain. | I swept and there's still sand in every corner. | Whose turn is it to fetch water?
b[spouses] : Yours. It's always yours. You know that.
b[child] : Not mine! I did it yesterday!
b : I'll help Restday. | It follows us in on our paws. | Yours.
a : You said that last Restday. | Sand and fur, everywhere. | I knew it.

scene ev_pl_field_long
when topic=smalltalk here.place=field
a : These rows go on forever. | Look how high the barley's grown. | Rest a moment under the oak?
b[farmer] : Rest's for winter. Bend your back.
b : Halfway now. | Good year coming. | Just a moment.
a : Halfway to forever. | Pray it holds. | Just one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Regions: Ridgemere

scene ev_rg_ridgemere_rain_forever
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
a : Has it stopped raining once this year? | I think I'm growing moss. | My shutters are swollen shut again.
b[old] : It stopped once. The summer I was nine. A Restday, I think.
b[child] : I like the rain. The gutters are rivers.
b : Not that I've seen. | Green suits you. | Kick them.
a : I don't believe it ever stops. | Mossy and miserable. | I kicked. Now my toe hurts.

scene ev_rg_ridgemere_sump
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=street|tavern|market
a : Don't take the Sump stairs after dark. | Someone lost a purse down in the Sump again. | The Sump smells worse than ever.
b[guard] : We patrol the Sump in fours now. Ask yourself why.
b : I never do. | Of course they did. | Something died, maybe.
a : Wise. | Never to be seen again. | Something always has.

scene ev_rg_ridgemere_houses
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
a : Greatly's wolves were strutting about the wharf. | Did you see House Mossgrave's banner over the wool shed? | The House wolves think the rain falls only on us.
b[noble] : The Houses keep this city alive. Mind your tongue.
b : Strutting like gulls. | Wool and more wool, everywhere. | It does fall only on us. Have you seen their roofs?
a : Gulls with purses. | Mossgrave wants every fleece in the Folds. | Slate. Fine slate.

scene ev_rg_saltreach_tide
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=shore|street|work|market
a : Spring tide tonight. | Salt in my fur, salt in my bread, salt in my dreams. | The gulls are thick on the salt pans.
b[fisher] : Bring the boats high. Spring tides take what's left low.
b : Watch the pan walls. | That's the wharf for you. | Something's dead out there.
a : I'll check them before dark. | All of it. | Always is.

scene ev_rg_serferro_gardens
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.season=spring|summer
a : The gardens up in the Heights are in flower. | Smell the cedars along the drive to Fellhall? | Lord Greatly's fountain is running again.
b[noble] : The gardens are open to the respectable. On certain days.
b : Lovely, aren't they. | Like summer itself, even in the rain. | For his guests, no doubt.
a : I'd like to sit in one. | I stand at the gate and breathe. | And never for us.

scene ev_rg_fortress_walls
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=gate|barracks
a : Same wall, same faces, every day. | Rain blows through these arrow slits all night. | Rations are thinner than they were.
b[guard] : Ask the Watch House for other duty, then. See where they send you.
b : That's the Watch. | Stuff them with rags. | Supply cart's late.
a : That's my life now. | I'd have to steal rags. | Isn't it always.

scene ev_new_rm_wharf
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=shore|street|work|market
a : The Fish Hall stinks worse than usual today. | Three boats in at once and the smokehouses are full. | Did you hear the bell at the Customs House?
b[fisher] : Stink means fish. Fish means coin. Breathe deep.
b : It always stinks. | Smoked fish for a month, then. | A ship in off the Sound, I suppose.
a : Worse, I said. | I'm not complaining. | Somebody's paying duty today.

scene ev_new_rm_rain_hall
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
a : The Council of Houses is sitting in the Rain Hall again. | They say the Rain Hall roof leaks right over the Council table. | Four Houses in one room. I'd not want to be the clerk.
b[official] : The Council sits when it must. Buckets and all.
b : Sitting and talking. | Fitting, in this city. | Nor me.
a : Talking and dripping. | They'll vote on a bucket. | He earns his ink.

scene ev_new_rm_heights
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=street|market
a : Pears at the Heights Market, a day's pay apiece. | Did you see the window at Silver & Rain? | The whole Heights smells of the Cedar Phial today.
b[noble] : Fine things for those who can afford them. That's what the Heights is for.
b : I'll stick to the Sump Market. | I saw the price card. | Better than it smells down here.
a : Porridge and pride. | So did I. I stopped breathing. | Most things are.

scene ev_new_rm_works
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=street|work|tavern
a : The Blue Vats have turned the gutter blue again. | Grayrock's foundry ran all night. I felt it through the floor. | The Fell Sawmill's been screaming since dawn.
b[laborer] : Work's work. A loud city's a fed city.
b[smith] : That's iron for half the country. Sleep through it.
b : Blue as a jay. | Like a heartbeat. | Plenty of logs coming down the Rainrun.
a : Bluer every week. | A hot one. | Plenty of noise, too.

scene ev_new_rm_grayrock_lord
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
a : Lord Grayrock's off up the High Road again. | They say Lady Maren hasn't left Grayrock Hall in years. | Young Tobias Grayrock was in the Slate & Ledger, buying rounds.
b[noble] : Lord Aldric goes where the iron is. The mines above Frosthollow, this time.
b : Again? He's never home. | Can't say I blame her. | Spending his father's iron.
a : Never. | Rain all day, why would she? | Iron melts quick, in a tavern.

scene ev_new_rm_commons
when topic=smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.place=street|market|home
a : The Commons Market had good cabbages today. | My little one starts at the Commons School next week. | The Grey Gull's put up a new sign.
b : Cabbages in the rain. Ridgemere. | Already? They grow so fast. | About time. The old one rotted.
a : Ridgemere supper. | Too fast. | Everything rots here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Regions: the towns and the country

scene ev_rg_cinderbrook_soot
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Soot on the snow again. | The smithy glows all night in this cold. | Picks ringing in the mine since before dawn.
b[smith] : That's the sound of good iron. Learn to love it.
b[miner] : Ore pays for the bread. Learn to love it.
b : You get used to it. | Pretty, in a way. | Never stops.
a : I never have. | Warmest thing in the valley. | Never.

scene ev_new_frosthollow
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Snow up to the eaves again. | The mine's swallowed the whole day shift. | A fire at the Frozen Lantern tonight, and I'm not leaving it.
b[miner] : Warmer down the shaft than up here, believe it or not.
b[old] : The Whitefangs keep their snow. Always have.
b : Dig the door out, then. | Lucky them, out of the wind. | Save me a stool.
a : Again. | Lucky? Down there? | Bring your own.

scene ev_rg_lake_mist
when topic=smalltalk here.region=lake
a : Mist sitting on the lake like a blanket. | Boats out early this morning. | The lake's glass-still today.
b[fisher] : Still water, no wind, no fish. Lake sulks like a wife.
b[sailor] : The mountains are hidden in that mist. I don't like it.
b : Pretty, isn't it. | They always are. | Good day for a swim.
a : Cold, though. | Lucky fish. | In Glasswater? Brave of you.

scene ev_new_coldwater
when topic=smalltalk here.region=coldwater
a : Glasswater's like a mirror this morning. | Put your paw in the lake. Go on. | They say the Long River starts right here.
b[fisher] : Cold water, sweet fish. Best in the country.
b[old] : The mountains feed that lake. It never warms.
b : Not a ripple. | I'd lose the paw. | Starts small, for something so long.
a : You can see the peaks twice. | Coward. | Everything starts small.

scene ev_new_oakhaven
when topic=smalltalk here.region=oakhaven
a : The Warmwood's humming today. Bees in every oak. | Acorns everywhere. The pigs are fat as lords. | A drink at the Acorn Inn after work?
b[woodcutter] : Warm wood, soft cutting. I'd not swap it for anything.
b : Warm enough to sleep outside. | Fatter than some lords. | Just the one.
a : I might. | I've seen thinner. | One. Then one more.

scene ev_rg_fens_peat
when topic=smalltalk here.region=fens
a : The peat smoke gets into everything. | Mist on the fens so thick I lost the path. | Will-o'-wisps over the bog again last night.
b[old] : Don't follow the lights. My brother did.
b[healer] : The fens grow every herb a healer needs. And some she doesn't.
b : I like the smell. | Follow the reed posts. | Marsh gas, nothing more.
a : It smells like home. | I nearly walked into the water. | Marsh gas that dances?

scene ev_new_mirebridge
when topic=smalltalk here.region=mirebridge
a : The Long River's up over the bridge stones again. | Eels in the traps this morning, thick as your arm. | The Eel and Lantern's damp as a frog's back.
b[fisher] : River gives and river takes. Mostly it gives eels.
b[old] : The fens were here before the town, and they'll be here after.
b : Mind the planks. | Smoke them, then. | Everything's damp here.
a : I always do. | Already on the rack. | Warm and damp. That's the Sallow Fens.

scene ev_rg_downs_hills
when topic=smalltalk here.region=downs
a : Sheep on every hill, as far as you can see. | The downs are gold in this light. | Wind smells of thyme up on the ridge.
b[herder] : And every one of them a fool. I love them.
b : Never seen so many. | Very fine. | Lovely.
a : Fools and wool. | It's a good country. | Makes me want to roll in it.

scene ev_rg_amberford_grass
when topic=smalltalk here.region=downs
a : Nothing but fields from here to the sky. | The wind never rests out here. | You can see a rider coming half a day away.
b[herder] : Good grass, fat herds. What else does a wolf need?
b : It's peaceful. | Hold onto your hat. | Gives you time to hide.
a : Too peaceful, some days. | Lost two hats this year. | Or to put the kettle on.

scene ev_new_larkfield
when topic=smalltalk here.region=larkfield
a : Market day again. The whole Larkdowns comes to town. | Hear the larks over the fields? | The Singing Lark's full of carters.
b[merchant] : Larkfield's built on market days. And bad bargains.
b[carter] : Every road meets here sooner or later.
b : Mind your purse. | All morning. | Full and loud.
a : Always. | Never tire of it. | Louder by night.

scene ev_new_southmeadow
when topic=smalltalk here.region=southmeadow here.season=summer|autumn
a : The orchards are heavy this year. | Grain as far as you can see. | Cider at the Apple Tree tonight?
b[farmer] : Heavy branches, sore backs. Best kind of year.
b : Good. Cheap apples. | Gold, all of it. | Just a cup.
a : Not for long. | Gold for someone. | A big cup.
